From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 04 Oct 2026 21:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ppc64 JIT: codegen, call-path and bound-branch fixes

Three independent sets of changes to js/src/jit/ppc64 plus small shared
fixes, measured together on a POWER8 (Octane 2.0 in the JS shell, on top
of the load64-immediate and veneer patches): 12812 -> 13820, Crypto +37%,
EarleyBoyer +15%, DeltaBlue +12%, RayTrace +13%, Gameboy +13%. jit-test
suite PASSED ALL, also with --jitflags=all.

Codegen (MacroAssembler-ppc64*.h, CodeGenerator-ppc64.cpp):
 - Value tag tests use sradi + cmpdi (tags all have bit 16 set, so the
   arithmetic shift yields a small negative constant) instead of
   srdi/xoris/cmplwi or srdi/lis/ori/cmpd; ma_cmp against an ImmTag is
   xoris + cmpldi; relational tag tests (GCThing, Double, Number,
   Primitive) compare the whole value against tag << 47.
 - Boxing an int32 is li/sldi/rldimi (3 insns, was 6); shifted-tag and
   magic constants load with li + sldi.
 - Overflow-checked add/sub/mul no longer re-sign-extend the result (the
   fall-through path already proves dest == extsw(dest)); and32/rshift32
   with immediates, add32(imm,src,dest) drop redundant mr/extsw.
 - Zero-offset BaseIndex loads/stores use the indexed forms; absolute
   address loads fold the low 16 bits into the displacement; andPtr with
   a high-run mask is clrrdi.

Call path (ppc64 + shared, ppc64-guarded where behaviour changes):
 - CodeGenerator-shared.cpp ensureOsiSpace emitted one 4-byte nop per
   padding BYTE on fixed-width ISAs (up to 40 nops after nearly every
   call where 10 were meant); step by NopSize(). x86 unchanged.
 - Ion/Baseline prologue is mflr/std/stdu/mr and the epilogue
   ld/mr/ld/mtlr/addi/blr with a single stack adjust each way; frame
   layout unchanged.
 - EmitPreBarrier tests the needs-barrier flag before saving LR.
 - Calls/jumps to trampolines within +-32 MiB are rewritten to bl/b at
   executableCopy time (Assembler::shortenNearJitBranches), the way
   arm64 does; only HARDCODED targets inside JIT memory are touched.
 - call(Register) emits b S; L: bctr; S: mtctr r12; bl L so the callee's
   mflr does not wait on the load -> mtctr -> bctrl chain.

Bound-branch fix (MacroAssembler-ppc64.h ma_b):
 - The bound short-branch displacement was computed before as_bc emitted
   its condition prefix, with a fixed -4 for every DoubleCondition.
   DoubleOrdered/DoubleUnordered emit no prefix (branch landed 4 bytes
   early); Overflow/NotOverflow emit 3 XER insns on POWER8 / mcrxrx on
   POWER9 (landed 12/4 bytes late). Now the prefix is emitted first and
   the displacement measured from the bc; the long form inverts the
   normalised BO bit instead of re-running the prefix. Latent in
   practice (Ion never emits such a backward branch), covered by a new
   jsapi-test (testJitMacroAssembler_ppc64BoundBranchPrefix) that fails
   before and passes after.

---
